ometry.\n- Pending footprint reservations, multi-tile queued object claims and save/restore coverage.\n- Merge against main af180e33f9, then against landed wheel fix f198f6d949, preserving main's controls and authored asset mapping.\n- Generated locale inventory preserves source-key quotations; shifted documentation anchors are repaired without relaxing test budgets.\n\nCurrent head: 71e25921a60c6359b04aca84fc17969a2586e3b2.\n\n## Obtained local evidence\n\n- Application and tools TypeScript targets: green.\n- Production build: green. Runtime atlas validator: 10 clips. Rendered-art validator: 40 catalog entries.\n- Twenty relevant unit/foundation files: 165 tests green.\n- After the wheel merge: eight relevant files, 52 tests green.\n- New merge regression: a restored full square with no construction history remains 64 pixels while a medical-bed structure retains its authored asset id.\n- Deliberately remove the production helper's asset-id spread: one test red, two green (expected asset id, received undefined). Exact byte restore SHA256 74F8F6D8B9F912FF562E80DA6274C2C36232004420C399215FAE87461F1DB6B0; four related files then 17 tests green.\n\n## Remaining gates and limits\n\nFull native Windows run at the first merge head completed with 495 passing files, 18 failing files; 5,760 passing tests, 49 failing tests and two skipped. This is not a full-suite pass. Failures include path separators, CRLF-sensitive scans and shell tests selecting unavailable WSL; an isolated main-based checkout reproduced the comment-symbol, composition-root and fenced-map failures. Hydrated published canteen pixels also exposed stale production calibration (191.4382 versus 209.852 red mean). The accepted root correction ea387a2e94 was extracted here. Restoring the old production means gives one real-PNG test red; exact restoration returns both tint suites to 23 green. The assertion, colours, opacity and contrast limits are unchanged.\n\nNo browser launched during this refresh. The earlier cancelled browser run is not acceptance evidence. Required exact-head verify/assets/browser checks must finish green, and the coordinator's new serial main CI after #1958 must finish green before merge.\n\nFactual evidence: docs/research/2026-10-02-room-template-dependency-main-refresh.md.\n\n## Browser coverage correction — 2026-10-02\n\nPublished checkpoint bfae195e74 replaces the six specific failures in terminal run37001303268 (760 passed /6 failed). The five viewport sweeps now visit every native plan control without new exemptions; native Tab checks include the separate plans action before/after filtering while retaining the catalogue's one-radio-stop assertions. Both production mutations fail, exact source restoration leaves zero production diff, and all six original cases pass locally. [Evidence](https://github.com/woogitsu/lockstate/blob/bfae195e74/docs/research/2026-10-02-room-plan-control-sweep.md). Fresh exact-head full Ubuntu CI and clean mergeability remain required; no full-suite or hosted acceptance claim.\n","created_at":"2026-10-01T16:50:34Z","updated_at":"2026-10-02T16:27:57Z","closed_at":"2026-10-02T16:11:48Z","merged_at":"2026-10-02T16:11:48Z","merge_commit_sha":"48da4ac330b43b8e2a8612d8dff160f2d380f05d","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[],"milestone":null,"draft":false,"commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/woogitsu/lockstate/pulls/1898/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/woogitsu/lockstate/pulls/1898/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/woogitsu/lockstate/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/woogitsu/lockstate/issues/1898/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/woogitsu/lockstate/statuses/bfae195e7470bf606b27dedfcf18c5f91d7703e0","head":{"label":"woogitsu:codex/review-template-footprint-1882-20261001","ref":"codex/review-template-footprint-1882-20261001","sha":"bfae195e7470bf606b27dedfcf18c5f91d7703e0","use